<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Capture Static Stripes</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Capture Static Stripes</span> <span lang="EN-GB">captures a single stripe from the ModelMaker sensor each time the '</span>B' button <span lang="EN-GB">is pressed. Press '</span>A' button to <span lang="EN-GB">terminate single stripe capture. This command is normally used to capture a surface profile in order to calculate certain angles by fitting lines.</span> This command is accessible from <span class="Path">System &gt; Performance Check Utilities &gt; Capture &gt; Static Stripes</span>.</p>
